/-!
# The étale cohomology spectral sequence of a ph hypercovering

Let `S` be a scheme, `X` an algebraic space over `S`, `U` a simplicial algebraic space over `S`
and `a : U → X` an augmentation which is a ph hypercovering. Let `𝓕` be a torsion abelian sheaf
on `X_étale` and `𝓕_p` its pullback to `U_{p, étale}` along `a_p : U_p → X`. Then there is a
canonical spectral sequence

`E₁^{p,q} = H^q_étale(U_p, 𝓕_p) ⇒ H^{p+q}_étale(X, 𝓕)`.

It is the ph cohomology spectral sequence of the hypercovering
(`AlgebraicGeometry.BigPHSpaceSite.phHypercoveringSpectralSequence`) at the pullback `a_X⁻¹𝓕` of
`𝓕` to the big ph site of `X`, along the comparison morphism `a_X` of Stacks 0DGW. The comparison
of étale and ph cohomology of torsion sheaves (Stacks 0DGV) identifies the abutment
`H^n_ph(X, a_X⁻¹𝓕)` with `H^n_étale(X, 𝓕)`, and, combined with the commutative square of
Stacks 0DGW, which identifies the restriction of `a_X⁻¹𝓕` to `(Spaces/U_p)_ph` with
`a_{U_p}⁻¹𝓕_p`, it identifies the first page `H^q_ph(U_p, (a_X⁻¹𝓕)|_{U_p})` with
`H^q_étale(U_p, 𝓕_p)`; the sheaves `𝓕_p` are torsion because inverse images preserve torsion
sheaves.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigPHSpaceSite.etaleToPhTopologyOver`: the pullback `a_X⁻¹𝓕` of an abelian
  sheaf on `X_étale` to the site in which ph descent is carried out.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigPHSpaceSite.phHypercoveringEtaleSpectralSequence`: the spectral sequence,
  as a functor of the abelian sheaf `𝓕` on `X_étale`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigPHSpaceSite.PhHypercoveringEtaleSpectralSequence`: the data asserted by
  Stacks 0DHP for one torsion sheaf: a spectral sequence, its first page and its abutment.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigPHSpaceSite.phCohomologyIsoEtaleCohomology`: `H^q_ph(Y, a_Y⁻¹𝓖)` is
  `H^q_étale(Y, 𝓖)` for a torsion sheaf `𝓖` on `Y_étale` (Stacks 0DGV, part (1)).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigPHSpaceSite.phHypercoveringEtaleSpectralSequence_pageOneIso`:
  `E₁^{p,q} = H^q_étale(U_p, 𝓕_p)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigPHSpaceSite.phHypercoveringEtaleSpectralSequence_abutsTo`: the spectral
  sequence abuts to `H^{p+q}_étale(X, 𝓕)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigPHSpaceSite.phHypercoveringEtaleSpectralSequenceOfTorsion`:
  **Stacks 0DHP**.

## Implementation notes

Étale cohomology is Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.functorH` on the spaces-étale site of
Stacks 03G0, and the abutment is extended by zero to the negative degrees. Ph descent is carried
out in the site whose topology is generated by the pretopology of the big ph topology
(`AlgebraicGeometry.BigPHSpaceSite.phTopologyOver`); this is the big ph topology itself, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigPHSpaceSite.toGrothendieck_toPretopology`, and sheaves and their cohomology
are carried between the two presentations by `etaleToPhTopologyOver` and
`rightDerivedΓObjIsoOfEq`. The ph site `P` and the étale site `E` of algebraic spaces are built on
the same big fppf site of schemes (`h : P.fppfSite = E.fppfSite`), as in Stacks 0DGW.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DHP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DHP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DGV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DGV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DGW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DGW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09WJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09WJ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite Stacks.CategoryTheory.Hypercovering
open scoped Simplicial

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.BigPHSpaceSite

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (P : BigPHSpaceSite S)

/-! ### The two presentations of the big ph topology -/

/-- The topology `phTopologyOver X` in which ph descent is carried out is the big ph topology
of `X`. -/
theorem phTopologyOver_eq (X : P.Spaces) :
    P.phTopologyOver X = BigPHSpaceOver.topology P X := by
  rw [phTopologyOver, toGrothendieck_toPretopology]

/-- A sheaf for the big ph topology of `X`, read as a sheaf for `phTopologyOver X`. -/
abbrev toPhTopologyOver (X : P.Spaces) :
    Sheaf (BigPHSpaceOver.topology P X) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} ⥤
      Sheaf (P.phTopologyOver X) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} :=
  ObjectProperty.ιOfLE fun _ hF ↦ hF.of_le (phTopologyOver_eq P X).le

/-- Cohomology of abelian sheaves on `Spaces/Y` does not depend on the presentation of the big ph
topology: for a topology `J` equal to the big ph topology and sheaves `F₁`, `F₂` for `J` and for
the big ph topology with isomorphic underlying presheaves, `H^q(J.over Y, F₁) ≅ H^q_ph(Y, F₂)`. -/
def rightDerivedΓObjIsoOfEq (J : GrothendieckTopology P.Spaces) (hJ : J = P.topology)
    (Y : P.Spaces) (F₁ : Sheaf (J.over Y) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})
    (F₂ : Sheaf (BigPHSpaceOver.topology P Y) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) (e : F₁.obj ≅ F₂.obj)
    (q : ℕ) :
    ((Sheaf.Γ (J.over Y) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}).rightDerived q).obj F₁ ≅
      ((Sheaf.Γ (BigPHSpaceOver.topology P Y) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}).rightDerived q).obj F₂ := by
  subst hJ
  exact ((Sheaf.Γ (BigPHSpaceOver.topology P Y) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}).rightDerived q).mapIso
    ((fullyFaithfulSheafToPresheaf _ _).preimageIso e)

/-! ### Étale and ph cohomology of torsion sheaves -/

variable (E : BigEtaleSpaceSite S) (h : P.fppfSite = E.fppfSite)

/-- The topology of the small étale site `Y_étale` of an algebraic space `Y` of the ph site. -/
abbrev etaleTopology (Y : P.Spaces) :
    GrothendieckTopology (Space.SpacesEtale E.fppfSite S E.fppf_mem (etaleSpace P E h Y)) :=
  Space.SpacesEtale.topology E.fppfSite S E.fppf_mem (etaleSpace P E h Y)

/-- **`H^q_ph(Y, a_Y⁻¹𝓖) = H^q_étale(Y, 𝓖)` for a torsion sheaf `𝓖` on `Y_étale`**: Stacks 0DGV,
part (1), with ph cohomology the right derived functors of `Γ((Spaces/Y)_ph, -)` and étale
cohomology Mathlib's sheaf cohomology. -/
def phCohomologyIsoEtaleCohomology (Y : P.Spaces)
    (G : Sheaf (etaleTopology P E h Y) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})
    (hG : Stacks.Torsion.torsionSheafProperty _ G) (q : ℕ) :
    ((Sheaf.Γ (BigPHSpaceOver.topology P Y) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}).rightDerived q).obj
        ((CategoryTheory.Sites.abelianInverseImage (phToSmallEtaleMorphism P E h Y)).obj G) ≅
      (Sheaf.functorH.{u + 1, u + 1} (etaleTopology P E h Y) q).obj G :=
  haveI := (Over.mkIdTerminal (X := Y)).hasTerminal
  haveI := (Space.SpacesEtale.final_isTerminal E.fppfSite S E.fppf_mem
    (etaleSpace P E h Y)).hasTerminal
  haveI : (Sheaf.Γ (etaleTopology P E h Y) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}).Additive :=
    Functor.additive_of_preserves_binary_products _
  (Functor.rightDerivedIsoOfNatIso
      (Sheaf.ΓNatIsoSheafSections _ _ (Over.mkIdTerminal (X := Y))) q).app _ ≪≫
    (etaleCohomologyIsoOfTorsion P E h Y G hG q).symm ≪≫
    (Functor.rightDerivedIsoOfNatIso
      (Sheaf.ΓNatIsoSheafSections (etaleTopology P E h Y) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}
      (Space.SpacesEtale.final_isTerminal E.fppfSite S E.fppf_mem
        (etaleSpace P E h Y))) q).symm.app G ≪≫
    (Stacks.Cohomology.GlobalSections.rightDerivedΓIsoFunctorH.{u + 1, u + 1, u + 1}
      (etaleTopology P E h Y) q).app G

/-! ### Restriction to `U_p` of the pullback of an étale sheaf -/

/-- **The pullback `a_X⁻¹𝓕` of an abelian sheaf `𝓕` on `X_étale` to the big ph site of `X`**,
read on the site `phTopologyOver X` in which ph descent is carried out. -/
abbrev etaleToPhTopologyOver (X : P.Spaces) :
    Sheaf (etaleTopology P E h X) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} ⥤
      Sheaf (P.phTopologyOver X) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} :=
  CategoryTheory.Sites.abelianInverseImage (phToSmallEtaleMorphism P E h X) ⋙
    toPhTopologyOver P X

/-- **The restriction of `a_X⁻¹𝓕` along `f : Y ⟶ X` is `a_Y⁻¹(f_small⁻¹𝓕)`**, on abelian sheaves:
the inverse image of `f_{big, ph}` is restriction along `Over.map f` (Stacks 0DFN), and the
second square of Stacks 0DGW identifies `f_{big, ph}⁻¹ ∘ a_X⁻¹` with `a_Y⁻¹ ∘ f_small⁻¹`. -/
def restrictionPhToSmallEtaleIso {X Y : P.Spaces} (f : Y ⟶ X) :
    CategoryTheory.Sites.abelianInverseImage (phToSmallEtaleMorphism P E h X) ⋙
        (Over.map f).sheafPushforwardContinuous AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}
          (BigPHSpaceOver.topology P Y) (BigPHSpaceOver.topology P X) ≅
      CategoryTheory.Sites.abelianInverseImage (E.smallEtaleMorphism (etaleMap P E h f)) ⋙
        CategoryTheory.Sites.abelianInverseImage (phToSmallEtaleMorphism P E h Y) :=
  letI : ((Over.map f).sheafPushforwardContinuous (Type (u + 1)) (BigPHSpaceOver.topology P Y)
      (BigPHSpaceOver.topology P X)).IsRightAdjoint :=
    (bigPHMorphismLowerShriekAdjunction P f).isRightAdjoint
  Functor.isoWhiskerLeft _
      (CategoryTheory.Sites.abelianInverseImageIsoSheafPushforwardContinuous (Over.map f) _ _
        (bigPHMorphism P f) (Iso.refl _)).symm ≪≫
    StacksTag03LR.abelianInverseImageSquareIso _ _ _ _ (bigPHSmallEtale_inverseImageCommIso P E h f)

/-! ### The spectral sequence -/

variable (A : SimplicialObject.Augmented P.Spaces)

/-- **The étale cohomology spectral sequence of an augmented simplicial algebraic space for the
ph topology**, as a functor of the abelian sheaf `𝓕` on `X_étale`: the ph cohomology spectral
sequence of `a : U → X` at the pullback `a_X⁻¹𝓕` of `𝓕` to the big ph site of `X`. -/
abbrev phHypercoveringEtaleSpectralSequence :
    Sheaf (etaleTopology P E h A.right) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} ⥤
      CohomologicalSpectralSequence AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} 1 :=
  etaleToPhTopologyOver P E h A.right ⋙ P.phHypercoveringSpectralSequence A

/-- **`E₁^{p,q} = H^q_étale(U_p, 𝓕_p)`** for a torsion abelian sheaf `𝓕` on `X_étale`, where
`𝓕_p` is the pullback of `𝓕` along the morphism of small étale topoi of `a_p : U_p → X`. The
first page of the ph spectral sequence is `H^q_ph(U_p, (a_X⁻¹𝓕)|_{U_p})`; the restriction is
`a_{U_p}⁻¹𝓕_p` by Stacks 0DGW, and its ph cohomology is the étale cohomology of the torsion
sheaf `𝓕_p` by Stacks 0DGV. -/
def phHypercoveringEtaleSpectralSequence_pageOneIso
    (F : Sheaf (etaleTopology P E h A.right) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})
    (hF : Stacks.Torsion.torsionSheafProperty _ F) (p q : ℕ) :
    (((phHypercoveringEtaleSpectralSequence P E h A).obj F).page 1 le_rfl).X
        ((p : ℤ), (q : ℤ)) ≅
      (Sheaf.functorH.{u + 1, u + 1} (etaleTopology P E h (A.left.obj (op ⦋p⦌))) q).obj
        ((CategoryTheory.Sites.abelianInverseImage
          (E.smallEtaleMorphism (etaleMap P E h
            (CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.augmentationApp A.left A.hom (op ⦋p⦌))))).obj F) :=
  (CategoryTheory.SimplicialSiteSituation.cohomologySpectralSequence_pageOneIso
      (CategoryTheory.SimplicialSemiRepresentable.totalSituation P.topology.toPretopology
        A.left A.hom) p q).app
      ((CategoryTheory.SimplicialSemiRepresentable.hypercoveringInverseImage
        P.topology.toPretopology A.left A.hom).obj ((etaleToPhTopologyOver P E h A.right).obj F)) ≪≫
    (CategoryTheory.SimplicialSemiRepresentable.componentCohomologyInverseImageIso
      P.topology.toPretopology A.left A.hom p q).app
      ((etaleToPhTopologyOver P E h A.right).obj F) ≪≫
    rightDerivedΓObjIsoOfEq P _ (toGrothendieck_toPretopology P) _ _
      (((Over.map (CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.augmentationApp A.left A.hom
          (op ⦋p⦌))).sheafPushforwardContinuous AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}
        (BigPHSpaceOver.topology P _) (BigPHSpaceOver.topology P A.right)).obj
          ((CategoryTheory.Sites.abelianInverseImage
            (phToSmallEtaleMorphism P E h A.right)).obj F)) (Iso.refl _) q ≪≫
    ((Sheaf.Γ (BigPHSpaceOver.topology P _) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}).rightDerived q).mapIso
      ((restrictionPhToSmallEtaleIso P E h
        (CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.augmentationApp A.left A.hom (op ⦋p⦌))).app F) ≪≫
    phCohomologyIsoEtaleCohomology P E h _ _
      (Stacks.Torsion.torsionSheafProperty_abelianInverseImage _ F hF) q

/-- **The étale cohomology `H^n_étale(X, 𝓕)` in integer degrees**: Mathlib's sheaf cohomology of
`X_étale` in the degrees `n ≥ 0`, and zero in the negative degrees. -/
abbrev etaleCohomologyZ (X : P.Spaces) (F : Sheaf (etaleTopology P E h X) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})
    (n : ℤ) : AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} :=
  if 0 ≤ n then (Sheaf.functorH.{u + 1, u + 1} (etaleTopology P E h X) n.toNat).obj F
  else AddCommGrpCat.of PUnit

variable {A} in
/-- **The spectral sequence of a ph hypercovering converges to `H^{p+q}_étale(X, 𝓕)`** for a
torsion abelian sheaf `𝓕` on `X_étale`. The ph spectral sequence abuts to `H^n_ph(X, a_X⁻¹𝓕)`
by ph descent along the hypercovering, and this is `H^n_étale(X, 𝓕)` by Stacks 0DGV; both
vanish in the negative degrees. -/
theorem phHypercoveringEtaleSpectralSequence_abutsTo
    (hA : MorphismProperty.IsHypercovering P.IsPHCoveringMorphism A)
    (F : Sheaf (etaleTopology P E h A.right) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})
    (hF : Stacks.Torsion.torsionSheafProperty _ F) :
    SpectralSequence.AbutsTo ((phHypercoveringEtaleSpectralSequence P E h A).obj F)
      (etaleCohomologyZ P E h A.right F) := by
  let G := (etaleToPhTopologyOver P E h A.right).obj F
  refine (P.phHypercoveringSpectralSequence_abutsTo hA G).of_iso fun n => ?_
  by_cases hn : 0 ≤ n
  · rw [etaleCohomologyZ, ite_eq_left hn]
    exact eqToIso (by rw [Int.toNat_of_nonneg hn]) ≪≫
      CategoryTheory.SimplicialSemiRepresentable.baseCohomologyIsoRightDerived _ G n.toNat ≪≫
      rightDerivedΓObjIsoOfEq P _ (toGrothendieck_toPretopology P) _ _
        ((CategoryTheory.Sites.abelianInverseImage
          (phToSmallEtaleMorphism P E h A.right)).obj F) (Iso.refl _) n.toNat ≪≫
      phCohomologyIsoEtaleCohomology P E h A.right F hF n.toNat
  · rw [etaleCohomologyZ, ite_eq_right hn]
    exact ((CategoryTheory.SimplicialSiteSituation.isZero_totalCohomologyZ_of_neg _ _ n
      (by omega)).of_iso
        (CategoryTheory.SimplicialSemiRepresentable.totalCohomologyZIsoBaseCohomology _ _ _
          (isHypercoveringAugmentation_of_isHypercovering hA) G n).symm).iso
      (AddCommGrpCat.isZero_of_subsingleton _)

/-- **The data asserted by Stacks 0DHP** for an augmentation `a : U → X` and an abelian sheaf `𝓕`
on `X_étale`: a spectral sequence with first page `E₁^{p,q} = H^q_étale(U_p, 𝓕_p)`, where `𝓕_p`
is the pullback of `𝓕` along the morphism of small étale topoi of `a_p : U_p → X`, converging
to `H^{p+q}_étale(X, 𝓕)`. -/
structure PhHypercoveringEtaleSpectralSequence
    (F : Sheaf (etaleTopology P E h A.right) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) where
  /-- The spectral sequence. -/
  sequence : CohomologicalSpectralSequence AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} 1
  /-- The first page: `E₁^{p,q} = H^q_étale(U_p, 𝓕_p)`. -/
  pageOneIso (p q : ℕ) :
    (sequence.page 1 le_rfl).X ((p : ℤ), (q : ℤ)) ≅
      (Sheaf.functorH.{u + 1, u + 1} (etaleTopology P E h (A.left.obj (op ⦋p⦌))) q).obj
        ((CategoryTheory.Sites.abelianInverseImage (E.smallEtaleMorphism
          (etaleMap P E h (CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.augmentationApp A.left A.hom
            (op ⦋p⦌))))).obj F)
  /-- The convergence: the spectral sequence abuts to `H^{p+q}_étale(X, 𝓕)`. -/
  abutsTo : SpectralSequence.AbutsTo sequence (etaleCohomologyZ P E h A.right F)

variable {A} in
/-- Let `S` be a scheme, `X` an algebraic space over `S`, `U` a simplicial algebraic space over
`S` and `a : U → X` an augmentation. Let `𝓕` be a torsion abelian sheaf on `X_étale` and let
`𝓕_p` be its pullback to `U_{p, étale}`. If `U` is a ph hypercovering of `X`, there is a
canonical spectral sequence

`E₁^{p,q} = H^q_étale(U_p, 𝓕_p)`

converging to `H^{p+q}_étale(X, 𝓕)`.

The spectral sequence is `phHypercoveringEtaleSpectralSequence`, the ph cohomology spectral
sequence of the hypercovering (Stacks 09WJ on the total ph site, with ph descent along the
hypercovering) at the pullback of `𝓕` to the big ph site of `X`; its first page and abutment are
identified with étale cohomology by Stacks 0DGV and Stacks 0DGW.

The source states the lemma for an arbitrary abelian sheaf `𝓕` and deduces it from Stacks 0DHM,
whose proof only covers torsion coefficients (it rests on Stacks 0DGU). As written, for all
abelian sheaves, the statement is false, and this is the corrected form, for torsion sheaves,
which is the form the proof gives. A counterexample with `𝓕 = ℚ`: let `X` be a normal surface
over an algebraically closed field with a cusp singularity `x`, let `X̃ → X` be its resolution,
with exceptional curve `E` a cycle of rational curves, so that `H¹_étale(E, ℚ) = ℚ`, and let `U`
be the Čech nerve of the proper surjective morphism `X̃ ⊔ {x} → X`, a proper and hence ph
hypercovering. Convergence of the canonical spectral sequence to `H^{p+q}_étale(X, ℚ)` is
cohomological descent for `ℚ` along `U`, which yields the Mayer–Vietoris sequence
`H¹(X̃, ℚ) ⊕ H¹(x, ℚ) → H¹(E, ℚ) → H²(X, ℚ)` of the abstract blow-up square; as `X̃` is normal,
`H¹(X̃, ℚ) = 0`, so `H²_étale(X, ℚ) ≠ 0`. But `H^i_étale(X, ℚ) = 0` for `i > 0` on the normal
scheme `X`. -/
@[stacks 0DHP]
def phHypercoveringEtaleSpectralSequenceOfTorsion
    (hA : MorphismProperty.IsHypercovering P.IsPHCoveringMorphism A)
    (F : Sheaf (etaleTopology P E h A.right) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})
    (hF : Stacks.Torsion.torsionSheafProperty _ F) :
    PhHypercoveringEtaleSpectralSequence P E h A F where
  sequence := (phHypercoveringEtaleSpectralSequence P E h A).obj F
  pageOneIso := phHypercoveringEtaleSpectralSequence_pageOneIso P E h A F hF
  abutsTo := phHypercoveringEtaleSpectralSequence_abutsTo P E h hA F hF

end AlgebraicGeometry.BigPHSpaceSite

end
